        "termsOfService": "https://isevenapi.xyz/",
        "title": "Is Even API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Check whether an integer is even or odd via a single GET request",
        "homepage": "https://isevenapi.xyz/",
        "docs_url": "https://isevenapi.xyz/",
        "license_short": "License not specified; copyright (c) 2020 Tanner.",
        "license_md": "- No explicit open-source licence is published on the API homepage.\n- The homepage shows a copyright notice: (c) 2020 Tanner.\n- Treat the service as a third-party hosted API; review the homepage before redistribution or commercial use.",
        "about_md": "The [Is Even API](https://isevenapi.xyz/) is a small joke/utility web service that answers a single question: is the number you sent even? It is hosted at `https://api.isevenapi.xyz/api` and is open to the public without authentication.\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- A single `GET /iseven/{number}/` endpoint that returns JSON.\n- An `iseven` boolean field indicating parity of the integer you passed.\n- An `ad` string field on the free tier, containing a sponsored message.\n\nThe documentation describes three tiers (Public/free, Premium, Enterprise) that differ in the maximum supported integer range; the free tier covers `0` to `999,999`. Negative numbers are supported. CORS is enabled, no API key is required for the free tier, and rate limits are not published.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "number_parity": "Represents the even/odd check for a single integer; served by `GET /iseven/{number}/` and returning a JSON object with an `iseven` boolean (plus an `ad` string on the free tier)."
